  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 258 PM CDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nHeavy showers with a couple rumbles of thunder continue Friday \nmorning through the afternoon hours. The upper-level shortwave \ntrough is expected to lift northeast throughout the day which will \npush scattered to numerous showers to the east and northeast parts \nof the region. Evaporative cooling and overcast cloud coverage \nlimits high temperatures to the mid 60s to mid 70s for most \nlocations. By Friday night, the shortwave trough shifts well east \nof the region. Subtle upper-level ridging builds in by Halloween \nmorning bringing mostly dry conditions throughout the day across \nthe area. Highs are expected to climb back into the 70s \nregionwide. Another upper-level system approaches from the west by\nSunday. This will bring low chances (20-40%) back in the forecast\nfor northern portions of the region. This system will eventually \nsend a cold front by early next week. Guidance does have the \nupper-low deepening across the Southern Plains by Tuesday which \nwill be a favorable pattern for breezy to strong winds, along with\ndry and cooler conditions by mid week. Uncertainty still persists\nin how strong winds will become, and how cool temperatures will \nbe. Stay tuned! \n\nLamberson",
